# Dockerfile-specific ignore file for .oss-scanner/Dockerfile
# (https://docs.docker.com/build/building/context/#dockerignore-files).
#
# This replaces the root .dockerignore for this build entirely (Docker does not
# merge them). The root file strips tests/ and *.test.js to keep the production
# image small, but this build runs `npm run test:quick`, so those must stay.
#
# .git/ is kept (unlike the exclusions below) because
# tests/unit/server/no-case-colliding-modules.test.js shells out to `git
# ls-files` to check for files that differ only in case; a git-less checkout
# makes that test fail outright, not just skip. The scan this image feeds into
# runs with no network access and its findings go only to primary_contact, so
# history embedded in .git isn't exposed beyond that private report.

.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.claude/

node_modules/
dist/
dist-bin/
client/dist/
build/
.next/
.nuxt/

logs/
*.log
contents/
coverage/
.nyc_output/

**/.env.production
*/.env
*/.env.*
!.env.example

.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*.tmp
*.temp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
